<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Cenbank bond rate rises to 2.5737 pct.</title>
<headline>Brazil Cenbank bond rate rises to 2.5737 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's benchmark overnight rate rose to 2.5737 percent a month, from 2.5445 percent last week, at today's 6.776 billion reais sale of 56-day Central Bank Bonds (BBC), dealers said.</p>
<p>The auction's result was in line with market expectations, they added.</p>
<p>The 56-day bonds will mature on March 5. Today's auction is expected to add 224 million reais to the banking system, with 7.0 billion reais in old bonds coming due Wednesday.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415))</p>
